  - Returns [38;5;153m{"status":201,"id":"ord_abcd1234"}[39m — while the write throws and nothing is stored. Silent write loss
    reported as success.
  - The rejection is unhandled, so under Node's default it [1mterminates the process[0m. Any client posting a bad [38;5;153mtotal[39m can
    take the service down. [38;5;153mparseOrderId[39m doesn't help — it validates [38;5;153mid[39m only, and nothing validates [38;5;153mtotal[39m.

  [1mImportant[0m

  1. [1mThe pagination test can't catch Critical 1[0m ([38;5;153mtest/handlers.test.js:26[39m). It asserts [38;5;153mres.orders.length === 10[39m; with 25
     seeded rows both [38;5;153mslice(0,10)[39m and the buggy [38;5;153mslice(10,20)[39m return 10. I ran the suite: [1m2 pass / 0 fail[0m on broken
     pagination. Needs assertions on contents and boundaries, not length.
  2. [1mNo happy-path test for order creation[0m ([38;5;153mtest/handlers.test.js:29-32[39m) — only the 400 branch. Half the commit's stated
